# Pomodoro (focus) timer

When editing Pomodoro timer code, follow the Guideline Index (`docs/GUIDELINE_INDEX.md`) entry for the Pomodoro timer.

Preserve these behaviors:

- **Single global tick:** One `setInterval` updates all running timers; start it when the first timer starts, clear it when the last pauses/stops/completes.
- **Work-only:** No break mode; on work completion reset to work (same duration) and optionally prompt "Mark task complete". Do not switch to short/long break.
- **Pause / resume:** On pause, set `sessionStartTimeRef[taskId] = Date.now() - elapsedSeconds * MILLISECONDS_PER_SECOND` so resume continues from the same remaining time. Clear the global interval before updating `isRunning: false` so no tick overwrites the pause. On play after pause, treat as resume when `sessionStartTimeRef` is set: keep `timeLeft`, call `runGlobalTick(taskId, false)` so the ref is not reset.
- **Same timer from card or dialog:** Task card and TaskDialog use the same timer id (task id or occurrence id); state is shared so pause on one and resume on the other works.

Use constants from `business-constants.ts` (POMODORO_*, SECONDS_PER_MINUTE, MILLISECONDS_PER_SECOND, STORAGE_KEY_POMODORO), `notification-constants.ts`, and `layout-constants.ts` (e.g. TOAST_DURATION_EXTRA_LONG_MS). Do not hardcode numeric or string business values.
